IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Public and Educational Lending Rights (Better Income for Authors) Act 2026
-- (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2026A00045.txt (as made; assent 20 May 2026).
-- The author or publisher asks: "Am I someone the Scheme pays; by when must I
-- seek reconsideration, and when is the Secretary taken to have affirmed; how
-- long must an overpayment notice give me?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 5 Australian person.
DECLARE `Residence` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `a permanent resident of Australia`
    `neither`

-- s 5 Australian creator: my contribution to the book.
DECLARE `Contribution` IS ONE OF
    `author of the whole or a part`
    `illustrator or translator of the whole or a part`
    `contributor of a significant proportion of original content`
    `none of these`

-- s 5 Australian publisher.
DECLARE `Publisher kind` IS ONE OF
    `a company incorporated in Australia publishing books in Australia`
    `a registered charity publishing books in Australia, meeting any rules`
    `an Australian creator who also publishes the book in Australia`
    `another person or body meeting the rules`
    `not a publisher`

-- ss 33-34: who made the reviewable decision.
DECLARE `Decision maker` IS ONE OF
    `a delegate of the Secretary`
    `the Secretary personally`

DECLARE `Lending case` HAS
    `I am`                                                  IS A `Residence`
    `I am an individual`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `my contribution`                                       IS A `Contribution`
    `as publisher I am`                                     IS A `Publisher kind`
    -- s 33
    `the decision was made by`                              IS A `Decision maker`
    `I was notified of the decision on`                     IS A DATE
    `the Secretary allowed a longer period ending on`       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the Secretary received my request on`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the Secretary notified the reconsideration on`         IS A MAYBE DATE
    -- s 38(2)(c)
    `an overpayment notice was given on`                    IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `Lending position` HAS
    `I am an Australian creator under s 5`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am an Australian publisher under s 5`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day to request reconsideration`               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the last day for the Secretary's reconsideration`      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the decision is taken to be affirmed under s 33(8)`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earliest last day an overpayment notice may set`   IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

-- s 5 Australian person and Australian creator.
@ref s 5
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am an Australian creator` c IF
        c's `I am an individual`
    AND NOT (c's `I am` EQUALS `neither`)
    AND NOT (c's `my contribution` EQUALS `none of these`)

-- s 5 Australian publisher; (c) needs an Australian creator of the book.
@ref s 5 Australian publisher
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am an Australian publisher` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `as publisher I am`
    WHEN `not a publisher` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an Australian creator who also publishes the book in Australia` THEN `I am an Australian creator` c
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 33(2): "before the end of the period of 28 days beginning on the day" I am
-- notified: notified + 27, or a longer period the Secretary allows.
@ref s 33(1)-(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last request day for` c MEANS
    IF c's `the decision was made by` EQUALS `the Secretary personally`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `the Secretary allowed a longer period ending on`
         WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (c's `I was notified of the decision on` PLUS 27)

-- s 33(5): "before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day the
-- Secretary receives the request": received + 89. Whether the request was made
-- in time is not checked: the encoding has no day the request was made (F6).
@ref s 33(5)
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last reconsideration day for` c MEANS
    IF c's `the decision was made by` EQUALS `the Secretary personally`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `the Secretary received my request on`
         WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d PLUS 89)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 33(8): taken to affirm if the person is not notified before the end of
-- that period.
@ref s 33(8)
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is taken to be affirmed` c IF
    CONSIDER `the last reconsideration day for` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the Secretary notified the reconsideration on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST n THEN n GREATER THAN lastday

-- s 34(1): the Secretary's own decision, or a reconsideration (made or taken).
@ref s 34(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may apply to the Tribunal` c IF
        c's `the decision was made by` EQUALS `the Secretary personally`
    OR  NOT (c's `the Secretary notified the reconsideration on` EQUALS NOTHING)
    OR  `the decision is taken to be affirmed` c

-- s 38(2)(c): a period "of at least 28 days starting on the day on which the
-- notice is given": it cannot end before the notice day + 27.
@ref s 38(2)(c)
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest notice end for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `an overpayment notice was given on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d PLUS 27)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref ss 5, 33, 34, 38
@export default The position of an author or publisher under the Public and Educational Lending Rights (Better Income for Authors) Act 2026 (Cth): whether they are an Australian creator (a citizen or permanent resident who wrote, illustrated, translated or contributed significant original content to a book) or an Australian publisher (s 5), whom the Scheme pays; for a reviewable decision by a delegate, the last day to ask the Secretary to reconsider (28 days beginning on notification, or a longer period allowed), the last day for the Secretary's reconsideration (90 days beginning on receipt) and whether it is then taken to be affirmed (s 33); whether they may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal (s 34); and the earliest last day an overpayment notice may set (at least 28 days starting on the notice day, s 38). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Lending case`  @desc My citizenship or residence, my contribution or publishing, and the decision, request, reconsideration and notice dates
GIVETH A `Lending position`
`the lending position for` c MEANS
    `Lending position` OF `I am an Australian creator` c, `I am an Australian publisher` c, `the last request day for` c,
                          `the last reconsideration day for` c, `the decision is taken to be affirmed` c,
                          `I may apply to the Tribunal` c, `the earliest notice end for` c
